# Just-in-Time Learning

Rather than reading every topic in advance, learn concepts when a project requires them.

For example:

* Need semantic search? → Learn embeddings.
* Need document-aware answers? → Learn RAG.
* Responses are slow? → Learn caching and batching.
* Hallucinations are a problem? → Learn evaluation and prompt design.
* Multiple specialized tasks? → Learn tool calling and agents.

This makes each concept immediately useful and easier to retain.

